    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Solves linear and integer programmes given as data (variables with objective and bounds, constraints in long format) with the HiGHS solver: optimal plan, slack, binding constraints and shadow prices.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Prescriptive",
    "tags": [
        "optimisation",
        "linear programming",
        "integer programming",
        "product mix",
        "allocation",
        "prescriptive",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Finds the **best plan** under constraints: the product mix that maximises profit within machine, labour and material capacity; the cheapest blend that meets a specification; the staffing that covers demand at least cost. The model is given as **data**, so planners can maintain it in a spreadsheet or database:\n\n**Input 1, decision variables**: one row per variable (product, route, shift) with its objective coefficient (profit or cost per unit), and optionally a lower bound (minimum, contract commitments), an upper bound (maximum demand) and a whole-number flag.\n\n**Input 2, constraints** in long format: one row per constraint and variable with the coefficient (for example hours per unit), plus the constraint's sense (`<=`, `>=` or `=`) and limit (capacity), repeated on each row.\n\nOutputs:\n- **Solution**: the optimal value of every variable, its contribution to the objective, whether it sits at a bound, and its reduced cost\n- **Constraints**: amount used, limit, slack, **binding** yes / no and the **shadow price** (how much the objective would improve per extra unit of that resource; continuous models only)\n- **Summary**: status (optimal, infeasible, unbounded), objective value, counts and the solver message\n\nUses the HiGHS solver in scipy (installed automatically through the block's dependencies).",
    "dependencies": "scipy",
